.TH DCC-CPU-CLI 1 2026-11-27 "Dudes Control Center @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
dcc-cpu-cli \- show and set CPU frequency settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcc-cpu-cli
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcc-cpu-cli
talks to
.BR dcc-cpu-daemon (8)
over
.IR /run/dcc-cpu.sock .
The user must be root or a member of the group
.BR dudes-control-center .
Without options it shows the governor, the frequencies of all cores and the
CPU package power with its sustained limit (from the kernel's RAPL energy
counter, measured by the daemon).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list\-profiles
List the custom CPU profiles with their index.
.TP
.BI \-\-apply\-profile " N"
Apply the custom profile with index
.IR N .
.TP
.BI \-\-governor " name"
Set the governor on all cores, for example
.BR performance ,
.BR schedutil ,
.BR powersave .
Which governors exist depends on the CPU frequency driver.
.TP
.BI \-\-hard\-limit " GHz"
Set the hard frequency limit (for example 3.8).
No core may run above it, whatever profile is active; the
.B dcc-hard-limit-enforcer
timer checks it every 10 seconds.
A limit is a ceiling: many CPUs do not go below a certain speed once they
have work to do, however low the limit is (see
.BR dcc-cpu-daemon (8)).
.TP
.B \-\-hard\-limit\-get
Show the hard frequency limit.
.TP
.BI \-\-battery\-limit " percent" "\fR|\fPoff"
Stop charging the battery at
.I percent
(50 to 100), or charge to 100 % with
.BR off .
Only where the battery driver offers a charge limit; the daemon stores it
and sets it again after a reboot or standby.
The status (no option) shows the limit as "Charge Limit".
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
Set the daemon's log level:
.BR ERROR ", " WARN ", " INFO " or " DEBUG .
At
.B DEBUG
the daemon also logs every query, such as the GUI's STATUS request every
5 seconds.
The level is kept until the daemon restarts.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level\-get
Show the daemon's log level.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error (daemon not reachable, invalid value, refused
command).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dcc-cpu-cli \-\-list\-profiles
.TQ
.B dcc-cpu-cli \-\-apply\-profile 0
Apply the first custom profile.
.TP
.B dcc-cpu-cli \-\-hard\-limit 3.8
Never run faster than 3.8 GHz.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dudes-control-center (7),
.BR dcc-cpu-daemon (8),
.BR dcc-gui (1)
